  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi alloy has a homogeneous single-phase FCC structure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 0.3–0.5 wt% Al to CoCrFeNi will trigger controlled nanoprecipitation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 0.3–0.5 wt% Al to CoCrFeNi will refine its grains to an ultrafine scale.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will develop a nanohierarchical structure containing coupled ultrafine grains and nanoprecipitates.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The precipitates produced by dilute Al addition will be nano-oxides.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At low temperature, the heterogeneous nanostructure will release frictional stress through multiple deformation pathways.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Low-temperature stress release through multiple deformation pathways will minimize adhesive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At high temperature, the nano-oxides will promote rapid tribo-oxidation and act as precursors to a dense nanocrystalline glaze layer.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A dense nanocrystalline oxide glaze can mitigate adhesive and oxidative wear at high temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide glaze will stabilize or reduce the coefficient of friction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC9960858::web::022::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al-modified CoCrFeNi will have a consistently lower coefficient of friction than unmodified CoCrFeNi from room temperature to 800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9960858::web::022::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al-modified CoCrFeNi will have a lower wear rate than unmodified CoCrFeNi throughout the range from room temperature to 800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC5706259::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unmodified CoCrFeNi exhibits especially high friction and wear at elevated temperature because of enhanced adhesive and oxidative wear.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sliding load and speed materially affect friction and wear behavior, so they must be controlled in the comparison.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::011::wear_analysis",
        "PMC9960858::web::022::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Environmental oxygen can support tribo-oxidation and formation of a protective oxide glaze during high-temperature sliding.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The comparison will use unmodified CoCrFeNi as a control and test both alloys at room temperature, approximately 400 °C, and 800 °C under identical sliding conditions.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Archard's law can be used to determine wear volume post-test.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure to obtain statistically significant reductions in both coefficient of friction and specific wear rate across the tested temperatures will falsify the performance prediction.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
